{
 "description": "The development gateway's Harbour fixture: what its DuckDB holds, under Snowflake's names. Owner choices it fixes. Dates: each portfolio answers from its own latest valuation (GLOBAL-CREDIT's is the 29th, 147HYC's the 30th); a portfolio's valuation dates are the same in POSITIONS_V and VALUATIONS_V, and every valuation holds at least one row, its cash at least; EM-RATES was first valued on the 30th. Keys: one row per position, Harbour summing a security's lots into it; cash is CASH-<currency>, with no ISIN; a derivative is its contract's id (an FX forward FXF-<pair>-<settlement date>, a CDS CDS-<reference entity>-<maturity>), a loan its facility's id (LN-<borrower>-<facility>), none with an ISIN; every ISIN has a valid ISO 6166 check digit. Values: market_value is in the position's own currency; a short (GLOBAL-CREDIT's Beta SA) and bought protection (EURO-IG's CDS) are negative; a position closed that day (147HYC's Treasury on the 30th) has zero quantity, market value and weight, its proceeds in cash. Weights and totals: each weight is the position's market value converted to the portfolio's base currency at FX_RATES_V's rate for the date, over the portfolio's total, so weights include cash, a short's is negative, and a portfolio's weights on a date sum to one; TOTAL_MV is that total in the base currency, rounded half-even to six places. Corrections: Harbour overwrites a valuation it restates, and LOADED_AT says when it wrote each row: GLOBAL-CREDIT's 28th was restated on the 30th. Times: LOADED_AT and CHECKED_AT hold UTC wall-clock times, a timestamp column's zone its third entry. Freshness: sources land once a business day (Monday to Friday, no holiday calendar) by 06:00 UTC the next day, and LOADS_V's check of 2026-10-31T06:00Z expects the 30th; each source's latest date is the latest its object holds; harbour.trades, which no capability here reads, is late. EURO-IG is closed.",
